Explanation of the change:

1. After we decide `onlyDisplay = true` (i.e. user’s raw input is either non‐numeric or out of range), we check specifically for “out of range” (`this.isGreaterThan(value, this.state.max)`).
2. If the new input is indeed > max, we simply `return` out of the handler, so neither the internal state nor the displayed value will change to the oversized number.
3. Existing blur‐time correction still applies in case the user manages to paste or otherwise sidestep this during composition.
